{
  "id": "qej7iM2JSaNNSpXE",
  "name": "WF-03 Operational Impact",
  "description": "Onward Phase 4: computes what a validated incident threatens downstream — dependency chain, affected operations, timing/urgency, service at risk — using real dependency-graph state (assets/locations/events + typed edges fetched from Postgres via the get_dependency_chain RPC), never AI. Calls decision-engine's /impact/calculate (pure function, no I/O) then persists to operational_impact. Idempotent — skips recomputation if impact already exists for the incident.",
  "active": true,
  "note": "Published and live-gate-tested (Phase 4). Real end-to-end runs through the real webhook -> WF-01 -> WF-02 -> WF-03 -> Supabase chain proved: baseline dependency chain with correct urgency (AV-204/ECON301, critical, 0-10min out); multiple downstream operations from one asset represented together (ECON301 + ECON301-EVENING); moving an event's start time later lowered its urgency from critical to low with no other change; changing attendee_count changed people_affected and the dependency_path text; deleting the ROOM-312->ECON301 edge made ECON301 disappear from affected_operations while ECON301-EVENING remained; an asset with zero dependency edges (HVAC-12) produced impact_known:false with no fabricated impact; re-invoking WF-03 for an incident that already had an operational_impact row took the Already Calculated? short-circuit straight to Existing Impact without calling decision-engine again or creating a duplicate row (verified via a temporary webhook trigger, added and removed for this one test). One real defect was found and fixed during this gate: WF-02's Fetch Prior Incidents had no alwaysOutputData, so an asset's first-ever incident (0 prior rows) silently skipped every downstream node including Trigger Impact — see wf02-incident-intelligence.json's note. 'Call Decision Engine' URL points at a Cloudflare Quick Tunnel (*.trycloudflare.com) — ephemeral, must be updated whenever the tunnel restarts, same as WF-02. Phase 5 addition: a 'Trigger Recovery' node fires WF-04 Recovery Planning fire-and-forget from Insert Impact's success output, mirroring WF-02's Trigger Impact pattern exactly — live-gate-tested (Phase 5 scenario A baseline ran the full real webhook -> WF-01 -> WF-02 -> WF-03 -> WF-04 -> Supabase chain end to end). Hardening checkpoint: 'Call Decision Engine' URL updated to the current Cloudflare Quick Tunnel after runtime cleanup. Added retryOnFail (3 tries, 1s wait) to Fetch Incident, Check Existing Impact, Fetch Asset, Fetch Intelligence, Call Dependency RPC (a read-only Supabase RPC call), Fetch All Locations, Fetch All Events, and Insert Impact -- Insert Impact is safe to retry because operational_impact.incident_id is a PRIMARY KEY, so a retry-after-actual-duplicate hits the existing constraint and falls through to the existing onError branch, never creating a second row (live node settings not re-serialized here in full; n8n is canonical per CLAUDE.md §9).",
  "settings": { "executionOrder": "v1", "availableInMCP": true },
